error[NK2101]: You're using `names` after a detached task took it.
  --> tests/async_detached_takes_what_it_uses.nika:7:2
   |
 7 | 	println(f"{names.len()} {h.join()}")
   |  ^
   |
   = note: A task started with `async(detached)` may outlive this function, so it takes the variables it uses with it. `names` is a `Vec[String]`, so it went to the task.
   = note: Numbers, `bool`s, views and `Shared[T]` handles aren't taken: they're copied.
   = help: Make a copy before and hand over the copy: `let copy = names.clone()`, then use `copy` inside.
warning[NK2123]: `spawn` is replaced by `async(detached)`, which starts the same task.
